"galaxigans_smoke.mst — drive GALAXIGANS with no window at all.

 The game is Smalltalk over GamePane, and every pane primitive is a documented
 no-op in a headless VM — so the whole thing (attract, the fire tap, the dive
 AI, bullets, bombs, collision, scoring, death and the game-over reset) runs
 and can be asserted on without a GUI. That is the point of the port: a game
 you can unit-test.

     dart --with-st macdart/st/test/run_mst.dart macdart/st/test/galaxigans_smoke.mst

 Prints one line per check and a final GALAXIGANS OK / GALAXIGANS FAILED — the
 battery (run_all.sh) greps for the OK."

| g fails check tap play |
fails := 0.
check := [ :label :got :want |
    got = want
        ifTrue: [ Transcript showCr: '  ok    ', label ]
        ifFalse: [
            fails := fails + 1.
            Transcript showCr: '  FAIL  ', label,
                ' — got ', got printString, ', want ', want printString ] ].
"One tap of fire: pressed for a frame, released the next. Holding does nothing
 (the original's no-autofire rule), so a test that never releases never shoots."
tap := [ GamePane stepWithKeys: 16. GamePane stepWithKeys: 0 ].
"n frames of play, tapping fire every 12 and sweeping left then right."
play := [ :n |
    1 to: n do: [ :i | | mask |
        mask := 0.
        (i \\ 12) = 0 ifTrue: [ mask := mask + 16 ].
        (i \\ 300) < 150 ifTrue: [ mask := mask + 1 ] ifFalse: [ mask := mask + 2 ].
        GamePane stepWithKeys: mask ] ].

g := Galaxigans launch.
check value: 'opens on the title' value: g gameState value: #attract.
check value: 'the fleet is full' value: g aliveCount value: 40.

1 to: 30 do: [ :i | GamePane stepWithKeys: 0 ].
check value: 'the title ignores an idle frame' value: g gameState value: #attract.

tap value.
check value: 'fire starts the game' value: g gameState value: #playing.

play value: 900.
check value: 'the fleet takes losses' value: g aliveCount < 40 value: true.
check value: 'and they score' value: g score > 0 value: true.
Transcript showCr: '  after 900 frames: ', g summary.

"Left alone against a FULL fleet, the divers reach the ship: three deaths, game
 over, and back to the title. The whole lifecycle in one loop, nobody at the
 keyboard. (A fresh game, because the fleet above is nearly cleared and eleven
 survivors take far longer to find a stationary ship.) Random is seeded 1, so
 this is the same run every time — the numbers below are exact, not typical."
g := Galaxigans launch.
tap value.
check value: 'a fresh game starts full' value: g aliveCount value: 40.
1 to: 2500 do: [ :i | GamePane stepWithKeys: 0 ].
check value: 'an idle ship dies out and resets' value: g gameState value: #attract.
check value: 'the reset refills the fleet' value: g aliveCount value: 40.
check value: 'and restores the lives' value: g lives value: 3.

Transcript showCr: (fails = 0
    ifTrue: [ 'GALAXIGANS OK' ]
    ifFalse: [ 'GALAXIGANS FAILED (', fails printString, ')' ]).
